       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 20 mg daily is double the FDA-labeled maximum of 10 mg once daily for adults. Doses above 10 mg raise the risk of peripheral edema, hypotension, and reflex tachycardia, and they usually add little blood pressure benefit.\n\nHere are some possible next steps:\n- **Amlodipine 10 mg PO once daily.** This is the standard maximum dose.\n- **Amlodipine 5 mg PO once daily, then titrate.** This is the usual starting dose. Some clinicians use 2.5 mg for frail patients.\n- **A second agent if 10 mg isn't enough.** An ACE inhibitor, an ARB, or a thiazide-type diuretic is the usual add-on.\n- **20 mg as written.** If you intentionally want this dose, for example on specialist advice, confirm that and tell me the rationale. I'll enter it with a note.\n\nWhich would you like me to enter?"
      }
